---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../components/SectionHeader.astro';
import Quote from '../components/Quote.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Our Story | Sarasudha — Music Across Generations"
  description="Discover the story behind Sarasudha, from the names Sarala and Sudha to its cultural roots in Annamacharya Kalabharati, Cuddapah, Regn. No. 217/1984."
  path="/our-story"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Our Story"
    title="A name born from family. A musical journey rooted in 1984."
    lede="Sarasudha takes its name from Sarala and Sudha — two names that carry ideas of simplicity, sincerity and sweetness. Its wider story reaches back to a cultural journey that began with Annamacharya Kalabharati in Cuddapah in 1984."
  />

  <section class="section name-section" aria-labelledby="name-heading">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <SectionHeader as="h2" id="name-heading" align="center" eyebrow="The Name" title="Sarala + Sudha → Sarasudha" />
      <p class="name-intro">Sarasudha is a name inspired by Sarala and Sudha.</p>

      <div class="name-transform">
        <div class="name-beat">
          <p class="name-beat__word">Sarala</p>
          <p class="name-beat__meaning">Simplicity. Sincerity. Grace.</p>
          <p class="name-beat__note">A name associated with being natural, direct and true.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="name-transform__operator" aria-hidden="true">+</div>
        <div class="name-beat">
          <p class="name-beat__word">Sudha</p>
          <p class="name-beat__meaning">Nectar. Sweetness. Richness.</p>
          <p class="name-beat__note">A name that evokes something life-giving and worth savouring.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="name-transform__operator" aria-hidden="true">=</div>
        <div class="name-beat name-beat--result">
          <p class="name-beat__result"><span class="name-beat__sara">Sara</span><span class="name-beat__sudha">sudha</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="name-copy">
        Two names from one family became the name for something intended to reach far beyond it.
        Sarasudha brings those ideas into music — honest in expression, rich in feeling and open to
        generations of artists and listeners.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="heritage-heading">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <SectionHeader
        as="h2"
        id="heritage-heading"
        eyebrow="Where It Began"
        title="Before Sarasudha, there was Annamacharya Kalabharati."
        lede="The story reaches back to Cuddapah in 1984, when Annamacharya Kalabharati was established as a cultural initiative centred on music and community."
      />
      <div class="registration-block">
        <p class="registration-block__name">Annamacharya Kalabharati</p>
        <p class="registration-block__meta">Cuddapah · Regn. No. 217/1984</p>
      </div>
      {/* P. Ramachandran's exact formal title is unverified — see docs/HERITAGE_VERIFICATION.md. Do not add a specific title here until confirmed. */}
      <p class="heritage-note">P. Ramachandran, the owner's father, was among its early leaders.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt" aria-labelledby="years-followed-heading">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <SectionHeader
        as="h2"
        id="years-followed-heading"
        eyebrow="The Years That Followed"
        title="The work continued across the decades."
      />
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          What began in 1984 continued through the years that followed. Family records point to
          community-supported cultural infrastructure, Annamacharya Jayanti and Vardhanti
          observances, and later efforts to protect what had been created.
        </p>
        <p>Those records are now being recovered and documented more fully in the Sarasudha archive.</p>
      </div>
      <a href="/heritage" class="btn btn-secondary years-cta">Explore the Heritage Archive</a>

      <div class="quieter-period">
        <p class="eyebrow">A Quieter Period</p>
        <h3>Some journeys have pauses.</h3>
        <p>
          In later years, the public programme became quieter. The performances and gatherings may
          have receded, but the records, memories and cultural intent remained.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="why-now-heading">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <SectionHeader
        as="h2"
        id="why-now-heading"
        eyebrow="2026"
        title="Not a return to the past. A new expression of its intent."
      />
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Sarasudha begins from that inheritance, but it is being built for today — for the way
          music is performed, discovered, shared and remembered now. It brings Carnatic tradition,
          light music, devotional expression and contemporary interpretation into one space, while
          creating room for artists and audiences to find each other.
        </p>
        <p>
          Music carries context most feeds strip away — the raga behind a composition, the story
          behind a performer, the tradition a piece draws from. Sarasudha is built to hold onto that
          depth while still reaching people where they already are.
        </p>
      </div>
      <Quote attribution="Sarasudha">
        Rooted in tradition. Open to every note.
      </Quote>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt" aria-labelledby="intent-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHeader as="h2" id="intent-heading" eyebrow="Our Intent" title="Preserve. Perform. Pass on." />
      <div class="pillars">
        <article class="pillar">
          <p class="pillar__index">01</p>
          <h3>Preserve</h3>
          <p>Document music, people, stories and cultural memory.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="pillar">
          <p class="pillar__index">02</p>
          <h3>Perform</h3>
          <p>Create spaces where music can be heard, experienced and reinterpreted.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="pillar">
          <p class="pillar__index">03</p>
          <h3>Pass On</h3>
          <p>Connect generations and encourage younger artists and audiences.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTA
    title="The story continues from here."
    lede="Explore the archive being built around Annamacharya Kalabharati, or find your own place in what Sarasudha becomes next."
    primaryLabel="Explore the Heritage"
    primaryHref="/heritage"
    secondaryLabel="Be Part of Sarasudha"
    secondaryHref="/participate"
  />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    font-size: var(--fs-300);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .registration-block {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
  }

  .registration-block__name {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-400);
    color: var(--color-maroon);
  }

  .registration-block__meta {
    margin-top: var(--space-1);
    font-size: var(--fs-200);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-accent-teal);
  }

  .heritage-note {
    max-width: 42rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--fs-200);
  }

  .years-cta {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  .quieter-period {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    padding-top: var(--space-7);
    border-top: var(--border-hairline);
    max-width: 34rem;
  }

  .quieter-period h3 {
    margin: var(--space-2) 0 var(--space-3);
  }

  .quieter-period p:not(.eyebrow) {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .pillars {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  .pillar {
    padding: var(--space-6);
    background: var(--color-warm-white);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    border: var(--border-hairline);
  }

  .pillar__index {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    color: var(--color-gold-text);
    font-size: var(--fs-400);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .pillar p:last-child {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  @media (min-width: 700px) {
    .pillars {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }

  /* The Name */
  .name-intro {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 32rem;
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-8);
    font-size: var(--fs-300);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .name-transform {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .name-beat {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 22rem;
  }

  .name-beat__word {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-700);
    color: var(--color-maroon);
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .name-beat__meaning {
    font-size: var(--fs-200);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-accent-teal);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .name-beat__note {
    font-size: var(--fs-200);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .name-transform__operator {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-500);
    color: var(--color-gold-text);
  }

  .name-beat--result {
    padding-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  .name-beat__result {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(var(--fs-800), 6vw, var(--fs-900));
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .name-beat__sara {
    color: var(--color-maroon);
  }

  .name-beat__sudha {
    color: var(--color-gold-text);
  }

  .name-copy {
    max-width: 38rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: var(--fs-300);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  @media (min-width: 700px) {
    .name-transform {
      flex-direction: row;
      justify-content: center;
      align-items: center;
      gap: var(--space-5);
    }
  }
</style>
